WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.267
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:06.868
We're hanging out with Savannah
Guthrie and Hoda Kotb!

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.300
You are two of the busiest
people on TV.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.234
Honestly, even when I'm lucky
enough to visit

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.033
the "Today" show, you're always
doing 10 other segments.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.400
So, like, our show, I can say
hello to you backstage.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.834
I got to see
your beautiful kids.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.200
I go, "Hi,
how are you guys doing?"

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.701
And your show,
you're like, "Hi, Jimmy."

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.200
And you're running off to do a
segment and running -- running.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.334
-It's crazy.
-It is a wild schedule.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.834
-I love the "Today" show
because of that.

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.334
There's just so much variety.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.534
But it's like,
"Here's Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.567
There's the Secretary of State.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.000
There's, like,
an albino elephant.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.934
-Everything around, yeah,
it's all happening.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:38.267
-Someone's doing a cartwheel.
Now there's a contortionist.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.868
-What time do you wake up
every morning?

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:43.801
-I do 3:15. I set my alarm
for 3:15 in the morning.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.934
-She has a whole ritual
she writes in her journal.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.567
-I know. I have to.
-She, like, smokes a peace pipe.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.033
-No, I don't smoke a peace pipe.
-You guys make it look so easy.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.834
And you go,
"Oh, they just look perfect."

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.234
And they wake up at 8:00
in the morning.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:56.601
Or 7:00, whatever --
This is unbelievable.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.801
3:00 in the morning?

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.901
-For her.
I used to get up at 3:00.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.434
But now I've been there
11 years,

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.434
so now I slack till 4:00.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.634
-Yeah. So that's why -- Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.534
-Do you ever get tempted
to hit snooze?

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.667
-Well, snooze is
a road to death.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.033
-Yeah, you can't --
If you hit snooze, it's over.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.367
You'll never make it in.
-If you hit snooze,

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.868
send your résumé. You're not
going to wake up again.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.000
-It's over.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.167
-It's the biggest button
on your alarm clock.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.334
-You got to ignore it.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.934
You know what? Never, ever.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.801
-Snooze, you lose.
You literally lose.

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:26.133
-Yeah.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.567
-I was looking for something
different that

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:29.901
no one's ever talked to
you guys about.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.701
And I found something that's
very interesting to me.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:34.934
You both are musically talented.
Musically gifted, I will say.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.667
[ Audience oohs ]
-No, no, we're not.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.300
-Let me finish.
This is the real thing.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.234
I heard that you both know
how to play guitar.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.100
-No.
-We know a few chords.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.267
-We know G, C, and D,
like 90% of America.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:50.901
-G, C, and D are all the chords
you need to know

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.334
when it comes to a guitar.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.334
And I thought since we are
"The Tonight Show,"

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:57.634
we're a very musical --
we have --

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:58.801
-Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.167
-We have guitars. Savannah.

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.400
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.701
-You're not even holding it.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.033
-I'm like, "How do we --"
-Hoda?

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.934
-So, like this, right? No, okay.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.300
-Is there another one? Oh, Lord.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.100
-Look at -- This is --
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.767
-I haven't touched a guitar
in six months.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.801
-Start with the Broadcast
and Cable Hall of Fame,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.434
next the Grammys --
That's what I'm saying.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.167
I want an album from you guys.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.834
-Is there, like, a fake Grammys,
like, the Whammies?

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:24.734
-What chords do you have?
What song do you both know?

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:27.167
Can we sing one?
-I don't have a pick.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:30.367
-Do you need a pick?
-Well, yeah.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.767
-Oh, I have picks.
I have picks for you.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.567
In fact,
I have Jimmy Fallon picks.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.767
-Oh!
-Wait, what?

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.033
-Aren't these cool?
-Thank you.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.767
-We're like, "We don't play.
Where's our picks?"

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:39.801
-Yeah, you're like, "Hey, guys,

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.200
where's our Savannah
and Hoda picks?"

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.067
-What's a G, C, D song?
-Wait, what chord is that?

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.200
-That's -- I only know --
this is -- Is this G?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.467
Or is it -- Wait, let me see
your finger.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.067
Yeah. Yeah.
-G.

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:51.400
We could do
"Blame It on My Juice."

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.701
-You're going to do Lizzo?

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.300
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.801
-Wait, you want to do --
Wait, which one? Oh, let's do --

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.667
-Roots, you can help out
whenever we know

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.200
what song this is.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:10.234
♪ -Almost heaven ♪

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:13.534
♪ West Virginia ♪

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.367
♪ Blue Ridge Mountains ♪

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:20.234
♪ Shenandoah River ♪

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.901
♪ Life is older ♪

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:26.434
♪ Older than the trees ♪

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:32.100
♪ Younger than the mountains
blowing like a breeze ♪

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.300
♪ Country roads ♪

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:43.567
♪ Take me home
to the place I belong ♪

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:44.734
-Come on!

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.000
-♪ West Virginia ♪

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.267
-Hit it, baby.

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.300
♪ Mountain mama ♪

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.601
♪ Take me home ♪

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.534
♪ Country roads ♪

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:59.934
-Not bad right there!
Savannah Guthrie!

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.167
Hoda Kotb, everybody!

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:06.033
Catch them on the "Today" show
weekday mornings here on NBC.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.767
We'll be right back
with Lily Collins.

